The B6 active and recovery subscriptions were created with Earliest initial position before the three records were published. After applying/ACKing 43/0 and creating the format-1 checkpoint, the recovery subscription sought after that checkpoint before the active source ACKed cut 44/0. Its no-ACK recovery cursor supplied the successor proof from the exact pair most recently delivered by that same guarded single-topic cursor; no arithmetic relation between ledger IDs was assumed. The isolated replay copy applied one record through 44/0, left 45/0 after the cut, and did not alter the original checkpoint or ACTIVE pointer.

This proves one cross-ledger transition in the ordered delivery stream of a retained P1 subscription and exercises one-entry ledgers. It does not prove recovery when required source records were deleted before the recovery subscription was opened, nor does it establish complete migration readiness, durable cutover/activation, rollback, old-reader retirement, central validation, or production authority. B6 remains IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION.

